@startuml
title PEP-28: Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server Architecture & Request Flow

actor "AI Agent / Client\n(Claude, Cursor, Script)" as Client
participant "AWS WAF / CloudFront\n(DDoS & Bot Shield)" as WAF
participant "EDI MCP Server\n(FastAPI / FastMCP)" as MCP
database "Amazon ElastiCache\n(Redis Cache & Quotas)" as Cache
participant "EDI Gatekeeper\n(Reverse Proxy)" as Gatekeeper
participant "EDI IAM\n(User Directory & Groups)" as IAM
participant "PASTA+ Core Services\n(Data Package & Audit Mgr)" as PASTA
database "AWS S3\n(Data Entities Storage)" as S3

autonumber

== Authenticated Request & Edge Bot Mitigation ==
Client -> WAF: MCP Request (JSON-RPC 2.0 via SSE/HTTP)\nHeader: X-API-Key: <EDI-API-Key>\nUser-Agent: EDI-MCP-Agent/1.0
note over WAF
  1. AWS WAF evaluates IP reputation & bot signatures
  2. Coarse volumetric rate-limiting drops scrapers
end note
WAF -> MCP: Forward authorized request

== IAM Tier Resolution & Quota Enforcement ==
MCP -> IAM: Validate API Key & Authorization
IAM --> MCP: Return EDI Token with IAM Groups\n(e.g., mcp-starter, mcp-team, mcp-power)
MCP -> Cache: Check per-tier rate limit & daily quota
alt Quota Exceeded
  MCP --> Client: HTTP 429 ("Tier Quota Exceeded - Upgrade at edirepository.org")
end

== Cache Evaluation ==
alt Read Request (Search / Metadata / Report)
  MCP -> Cache: Check cache (hash key of endpoint + params)
  alt Cache Hit
    Cache --> MCP: Return cached XML / JSON payload
    MCP --> Client: Tool/Resource response (0 backend load)
  end
end

== Backend Dispatch to PASTA+ ==
MCP -> Gatekeeper: REST Request + EDI Token\nHeader: User-Agent: EDI-MCP-Agent/1.0\nHeader: EDI-Agent-Client-ID: <id>
Gatekeeper -> PASTA: Authorized REST call with EDI Token

== Response Handling & Raw Streaming ==
alt Small Payload (Search results, XML metadata, JSON)
  PASTA --> Gatekeeper: REST XML / JSON response
  Gatekeeper --> MCP: REST response
  MCP -> Cache: Cache response (TTL: 1h - 24h)
  MCP --> Client: Tool response (JSON-RPC)
else Large Data Entity (readDataEntity)
  PASTA --> Gatekeeper: Stream data stream / chunked transfer
  Gatekeeper --> MCP: Pipe raw byte stream (no memory buffering)
  MCP --> Client: Stream raw bytes (client LLM handles budgeting/truncation)
end

@enduml
